CompCert follows each dependency once, ignores nested comments and external
standard-library theories, and puts Flocq in its own theory.

  $ mkdir -p compcert-base/lib compcert-base/common compcert-base/x86_64 compcert-base/x86 compcert-base/cfrontend compcert-base/flocq
  $ for file in cfrontend/Ctyping.v common/Globalenvs.v common/Memory.v; do
  >   echo '(* GNU Lesser General Public License *)' > "compcert-base/$file"
  > done
  $ cp -R compcert-base compcert-upstream
  $ cat >> compcert-upstream/cfrontend/Ctyping.v <<'COQ'
  > Require Import Globalenvs Memory.
  > (* outer comment
  >    (* nested comment *) Require Import Forbidden.
  > *)
  > From Flocq.Core Require Export Fcore.
  > COQ
  $ echo 'Require Memory.' >> compcert-upstream/common/Globalenvs.v
  $ cat >> compcert-upstream/common/Memory.v <<'COQ'
  > From Stdlib Require Import List.
  > From Corelib Require Import Nat.
  > From Coq Require Import Bool.
  > Require Import Utilé.
  > COQ
  $ mkdir -p compcert-upstream/flocq/Core
  $ echo '(* GNU Lesser General Public License *)' > compcert-upstream/flocq/Core/Fcore.v
  $ echo '(* No LGPL header; outside the dependency closure. *)' > compcert-upstream/lib/Unused.v
  $ cat > compcert-upstream/lib/Utilé.v <<'COQ'
  > (* GNU Lesser General Public License *)
  > Require Export Ctyping.
  > COQ
  $ bun gen-dune.ts compcert compcert-upstream
  ; Generated by test/compcert/gen-dune.ts; only audited LGPL sources.
  ; x86-64 parameters are fixed independently of the host architecture.
  (subdir compcert
   (dirs lib common x86_64 x86 cfrontend flocq selected)
   (subdir selected
    (include_subdirs qualified)
    (subdir lib (copy_files ../../lib/Utilé.v))
  (subdir common (copy_files ../../common/Globalenvs.v) (copy_files ../../common/Memory.v))
  (subdir x86_64 )
  (subdir x86 )
  (subdir cfrontend (copy_files ../../cfrontend/Ctyping.v))
    (rocq.theory
     (name compcert)
     (modules cfrontend.Ctyping common.Globalenvs common.Memory lib.Utilé)
     (flags :standard -w -deprecated,-register-all)
     (theories Stdlib Flocq)))
   (subdir flocq
    (include_subdirs qualified)
    (rocq.theory
     (name Flocq)
     (modules Core.Fcore)
     (flags :standard -w -deprecated)
     (theories Stdlib))))

CompCert rejects dependencies that do not exist.

  $ rm -rf compcert-upstream
  $ cp -R compcert-base compcert-upstream
  $ echo 'Require Missing.' >> compcert-upstream/cfrontend/Ctyping.v
  $ bun gen-dune.ts compcert compcert-upstream
  Unknown CompCert module: Missing
  [1]

CompCert rejects sources outside the audited subset, even with an LGPL header.

  $ rm -rf compcert-upstream
  $ cp -R compcert-base compcert-upstream
  $ echo 'Require Forbidden.' >> compcert-upstream/cfrontend/Ctyping.v
  $ echo '(* GNU Lesser General Public License *)' > compcert-upstream/cfrontend/Forbidden.v
  $ bun gen-dune.ts compcert compcert-upstream
  Not in the audited LGPL subset: cfrontend/Forbidden.v
  [1]

CompCert rejects approved paths that lack an LGPL header.

  $ rm -rf compcert-upstream
  $ cp -R compcert-base compcert-upstream
  $ echo '(* No license header. *)' > compcert-upstream/common/Memory.v
  $ bun gen-dune.ts compcert compcert-upstream
  Not in the audited LGPL subset: common/Memory.v
  [1]

CompCert rejects ambiguous module names.

  $ rm -rf compcert-upstream
  $ cp -R compcert-base compcert-upstream
  $ echo '(* GNU Lesser General Public License *)' > compcert-upstream/lib/Memory.v
  $ bun gen-dune.ts compcert compcert-upstream
  Ambiguous module: Memory
  [1]

Fiat Crypto follows both namespaces, ignores nested comments and external
theories, and excludes sources outside the dependency closure.

  $ mkdir -p fiat-crypto/rewriter/src/Rewriter fiat-crypto/src/Arithmetic
  $ echo 'From Crypto Require Export Alpha.' > fiat-crypto/rewriter/src/Rewriter/Util.v
  $ echo 'Require Crypto.Arithmetic.ModOps.' > fiat-crypto/src/Alpha.v
  $ cat > fiat-crypto/src/Arithmetic/ModOps.v <<'COQ'
  > (* outer comment
  >    (* nested comment *) Require Import Crypto.Missing.
  > *)
  > From Crypto Require Import Zeta Alpha Épsilon.
  > Require Export Rewriter.Util.
  > From Stdlib Require Import List.
  > COQ
  $ echo 'Require Crypto.Missing.' > fiat-crypto/src/Unused.v
  $ echo 'From Rewriter Require Import Util.' > fiat-crypto/src/Zeta.v
  $ touch fiat-crypto/src/Épsilon.v
  $ bun gen-dune.ts fiat-crypto fiat-crypto | sed '/^[[:space:]]*$/d'
  ; Generated by gen-dune.ts from the pinned upstream sources.
  ; Compile the dependency closure unchanged, including its proofs.
  (subdir
   fiat-crypto
   (dirs src rewriter)
   (subdir
    rewriter
    (dirs src)
    (subdir
     src/Rewriter
  (include_subdirs qualified)
  (rocq.theory
   (name Rewriter)
   (modules Util)
   (theories Stdlib))
  ))
   (subdir
    src
  (include_subdirs qualified)
  (rocq.theory
   (name Crypto)
   (modules Alpha
  Arithmetic.ModOps
  Zeta
  Épsilon)
   (theories Stdlib Rewriter))
  ))

Fiat Crypto rejects missing sources in either namespace.

  $ rm -rf fiat-crypto
  $ mkdir -p fiat-crypto/src/Arithmetic
  $ echo 'Require Import Crypto.Missing.' > fiat-crypto/src/Arithmetic/ModOps.v
  $ bun gen-dune.ts fiat-crypto fiat-crypto
  ENOENT: no such file or directory, open 'fiat-crypto/src/Missing.v'
  [1]
  $ echo 'Require Import Rewriter.Missing.' > fiat-crypto/src/Arithmetic/ModOps.v
  $ bun gen-dune.ts fiat-crypto fiat-crypto
  ENOENT: no such file or directory, open 'fiat-crypto/rewriter/src/Rewriter/Missing.v'
  [1]
